        <notes>
            <note>The Oxford, Las Vegas and one of the Levy copies are bound with </note>
            <note rend="italic">Le Jeu des Échecs, Traduit de l'Italien de Giachino Greco, Calabrois. Nouvelle Edition. </note>
            <note>A Paris, Chez les Libraires Associés (1774). The book was reissued with a cancel title in 1781 without the added chess book.</note>
            <note rend="paragraph"/>
            <note>The other Levy copy has </note>
            <note rend="italic">Le Jeu de Whist, Satyre. </note>
            <note>A Paris, Chez Léopold Collin (1807) bound between the sections on whist and trois-sept. After trois-sept is a second unidentified book on the game, </note>
